      "answer": "Based on my research, I found the information about the quaystone library's retry ceiling change:\n\nThe change occurred in version 4.2.0 of the quaystone library. \n\nWhat changed: The retry ceiling now counts attempts rather than retries. This means that a configuration setting that previously specified \"6\" would now mean \"7\" attempts. In other words, if you had a retry ceiling of 6 before this change, it would now allow 7 total attempts (1 initial attempt + 6 retries), whereas before it only allowed 6 retries.\n\nThis was documented in the changelog where it states: \"The retry ceiling now counts attempts rather than retries. A config that said 6 before means 7 now.\"",
